<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pangkalan Bun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pangkalan Bun is a town on the Arut river in Central Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, in the south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>. The court of the Kotawaringin Sultanate moved there from Kotawaringin Lama in the early 19th century, and the wooden royal palace, the Istana Kuning, still stands. It is now the seat of West Kotawaringin Regency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pangkalan-bun.jpg" alt="Pangkalan Bun" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simon Liem · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pangkalan_Bun.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
